tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why children are last to be treated in medical crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dda8a68e23dab0b78947efb8108815edb9e8b68fd1cc1b152a2bad3b773f624c</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107--c059b44b485e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo, children are more likely to die than adults. But it's not always due to the disease. Specific medicines for younger people are often harder to come by.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00f147cfeeda928286af830e7e33232eab3af7acc9cda4c7c760580e8484948</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why many Syrians feel Assad death sentence isn't enough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1efb98569ac8bf0a0290343002f84d51a3182134346180099829cc0d219fd610</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915--4ab418802105.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In July, a Syrian court sentenced former dictator Bashar Assad to death for crimes against his own people. But after 14 years of civil war, many survivors are demanding more when it comes to transitional justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d93e193f1aa0443bf0d750198f587a3947112c4903b99ac8670eaddb0d2f395e</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting intensifies amid Houthi push in the west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4755d2c889b1d240300a655b96cdd6d3a8dce6f835be6ce3fa3d97ca16e671c8</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588--651aa6fc20cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-fighting-intensifies-amid-houthi-push-in-the-west/a-79039588?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces are trying to secure high ground and solidify their control of the entry to the Red Sea in the southwest. The Iran-backed militia abandoned a shaky truce with the Saudi-backed government-in-exile in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Suspected oil thieves dead after inhaling fumes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:955781ffec6134466697e2de89fbc1f52d67c0a490a23ccedd56a25c84f4f09f</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997--76c34d7b815f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-suspected-oil-thieves-dead-after-inhaling-fumes/a-79001997?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Nigerian environmental group says that at least 37 people died trying to siphon crude oil off a ship illegally. Police acknowledged a fatal incident but gave fewer details, saying investigations continued.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood disaster puts climate justice under spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9afdff2a6a865ab0a7becc6729c38ffd58fd2e2c443e3caf24d0f457a3aa5090</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-puts-climate-justice-under-spotlight/a-78998617--8f177ec379f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-disaster-puts-climate-justice-under-spotlight/a-78998617?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The devastating Himalayan glacial floods have raised broader questions about who should bear the costs and responsibility for the impacts of climate-related disasters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How can African retailers compete with Shein and Temu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c3d9bdcb31d1dfb4293ad2e0302f364d16e3f51cc14832b1fd9fbbe172acf01</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195--3bda9e77e49f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-can-african-retailers-compete-with-shein-and-temu/a-78988195?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shein and Temu are expanding across Africa with low prices and vast product ranges. Businesses and unions warn the growth could come at a cost for local jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: How the funeral of Ratko Mladic is dividing a nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0ad503811809e53f6071d7c729e01412e8203620bb767b308f4acff6832a1d1</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890--47086bf0a8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the Serbian government leaves the decision about Ratko Mladic's funeral arrangements to his family, international pressure on the country is mounting. How do Serbs feel about the matter?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
